     "normal+enchanted: RealmSpeak MagicRealmData.xml, github.com/dewkid/RealmSpeak branch master (commit 8b1d9ab5d5a310b856ed88ce9059ca549ce0b08c), path magic_realm/utility/components/resources/data/MagicRealmData.xml, sha1 30bcaf3fe8875e4039fc19ad38f9da8a6567636a",
     "topology cross-check (identical for all 20 tiles, both sides): github.com/sch4fchen/RealmSpeak fork, same path; it is a fork, so not independent evidence",
     "normal side cross-check only: prototype /Users/tharkad/casdra/magic-realm-server/mr-tiles.json (see docs/data/tiles-diff.md)",
     "rules cross-check: magic-realm/docs/rules/02_map_movement_hiding.md sections 2, 3, 6.3"
   ],
   "edgeNames": [
     "N",
     "NE",
     "SE",
     "S",
     "SW",
     "NW"
   ],
   "notes": "Topology only; no geometry. Data is RealmSpeak values; nothing was corrected by symmetry. RealmSpeak types clearings woods/mountain/caves/normal: caves -> \"cave\", normal -> \"woods\" (the \"normal\" label is used on every Valley clearing, all Ruins clearings but 6, and Borderland enchanted clearing 1; the research notes count them as woods). Path kinds: RealmSpeak normal -> open, caves -> tunnel. Enchanted colour letters R=grey, G=gold, P=purple. \"bridge\" is not present in RealmSpeak topology data; it is false except as described below. edges maps compass edge of the tile as printed (name along the S edge) to the clearing number the edge road leaves from; the prototype edge numbers 1..6 map to NE,SE,S,SW,NW,N respectively (verified in tiles-diff.md). Each side lists each road once with a<b. Bridges: RealmSpeak has no bridge attribute; bridge=true is set only for Ledges normal side 2-5 (research notes 02 section 3, from the 3E tile illustration: the 2-5 road bridges over the 4-N road). RealmSpeak xy/arc points put 2-5 and 4-N in crossing position on the Ledges enchanted side too, and several other pairs cross geometrically (Valley 1-4 vs 2-5, Borderland, High Pass): those are NOT marked and are listed as OPEN in tiles-diff.md."
 },
